        "name": "USN-8630-5",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - x86 architecture;   - InfiniBand drivers;   - Network drivers;   - Mellanox network drivers;   - File systems infrastructure;   - IPv4 networking;   - Network traffic control;   - TCP network protocol;   - B.A.T.M.A.N. meshing protocol;   - IPv6 networking;   - Multipath TCP;   - Netfilter;   - RxRPC session sockets;   - SCTP protocol;   - SMC sockets; (CVE-2026-43083, CVE-2026-43197, CVE-2026-43198, CVE-2026-43465, CVE-2026-46242, CVE-2026-46325, CVE-2026-46331, CVE-2026-52914, CVE-2026-52924, CVE-2026-52931, CVE-2026-53151, CVE-2026-53176, CVE-2026-53212, CVE-2026-53215, CVE-2026-53225, CVE-2026-53228, CVE-2026-53359)",
